    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the bleed isolation valve installation at the two engine positions, the cross-bleed position and the ground connection, with the pre and post modification duct and sensor items.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "To identify the parts of the bleed isolation valve installation at all four valve positions, including the duct and sensor items that changed at the four-position standard.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left and right engine positions viewed from below with the fan cowl open; sheet 2 shows the cross-bleed and ground connection positions in the belly fairing. Item 20 and item 20A are the cross-bleed duct before and after the four-position standard: the later duct carries the sensor mounting boss and the two are not interchangeable in either direction. They were listed as one item with a note until this issue, and the note was not enough, because the item number is what the line orders against and the note is not. Item 40, the position sensor, exists only on aircraft at the four-position standard, and four are fitted. The regulator at item 30 is common to all four positions from the four-position standard onward; before that the cross-bleed and ground connection positions carried a different regulator that is no longer supplied."
    },
